Siphosethu,

Gerhard Smit here, CTTX in Gqeberha. We engineer owned networks on wind farms=
, reserves and remote sites; we don't sell packages.

On a renewable plant the network question is resilience: when the fibre
is cut or stolen, does SCADA stay up, can the O&M crews still work across
the site, and are the perimeter cameras still reporting? A standby
wireless path that takes over automatically costs far less than one day of
lost visibility. We have done this kind of work at Oya Wind Farm and at Eskom=
 Medupi.

I'd like to run a desk study on ENGIE from terrain and public
infrastructure data first: where a backbone can run across the site and
how a reliable uplink gets onto it. It tells you what is feasible before
anyone spends money.

If that's useful, the next step is a half-day assessment on site: what you
have, what fails, what it costs you, and what an owned network would look
like. R3,500 ex VAT, credited against the build, and the report is yours
either way. The one-page proposal is attached; the short version is here:
www.cttx.co.za/assessment

Can I call you for 10 minutes this week?

Gerhard Smit
Director | CTTX Services (Pty) Ltd
gerhard@cttx.co.za | 041 371 1089 | 084 550 3281
www.cttx.co.za

If this isn't relevant to you, reply "no thanks" and I won't follow up.

